+# ChatGPT project-agent distribution
+
+This directory owns the reviewable sources and generated small tools payload for
+agents running inside the TeaseScript ChatGPT project. It does not define Codex
+or generic local-agent policy. After an exact checkout exists, repository-local
+instructions are authoritative.
+
+## Canonical sources
+
+- `project-files/README-FIRST.template.md` is the stable canonical successor for
+  the former project-folder `PROJECT-INSTRUCTIONS.txt`, workflow-context, and
+  bootstrap-guide files. The generated project `README-FIRST.md` consolidates
+  those startup concerns to keep the external folder below the five-file limit.
+- `CODEX-MODEL-REASONING-SELECTION.md` owns the complete model/reasoning guide;
+  the generated project README carries its compact startup summary.
+- `PROJECT-SYSTEM-PROMPT.txt` is the canonical text copied manually into the
+  separate ChatGPT project instruction/system-prompt field. It is deliberately
+  absent from project-folder files and both archives.
+- `tools-root/` and the repository files named by `SOURCE_FILES` in
+  `build-tools-bundle.py` are the editable tools-bundle sources.
+- `bundle/teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent-tools-linux-x64.tar.zst` is a
+  committed deterministic derivative. Do not edit it directly.
+- `setup-teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent.py` safely assembles that tools bundle
+  with the separately managed large runtime payload.
+
+The external runtime payload is not committed to Git because it is about 100 MB
+and changes rarely. `prepare-runtime-payload.py` derives it from a verified
+legacy bootstrap release. Small text or script changes never require rebuilding
+or replacing that runtime.
+
+## Build and verify
+
+```bash
+python3 -B tools/chatgpt-project-agent/build-tools-bundle.py
+python3 -B tools/chatgpt-project-agent/test-chatgpt-project-agent.py
+```
+
+The tools bundle uses deterministic `tar.zst` with zstd ultra level 22 because
+its input is small. Runtime preparation defaults to zstd level 9: still high
+compression, but practical for the approximately 100 MB binary/cache payload.
+XZ is not a distribution format: the current tools benchmark saves only 9
+bytes versus `tar.zst`, while a second archive format and its costly large-payload
+compression would add complexity without a useful project-folder benefit.
+
+Known aggregate checks and archive work can exceed short harness defaults. Set
+an explicit extended timeout before invoking them; normally allow at least 120
+seconds for the aggregate local-agent suite and more for measured runtime
+compression or full repository verification.
+
+## Prepare the external project files
+
+```bash
+python3 -B tools/chatgpt-project-agent/prepare-runtime-payload.py \
+  --bootstrap-archive /path/to/teasescript-agent-bootstrap-linux-x64.tar.zst \
+  --bootstrap-sha256 <sha256> \
+  --output /tmp/teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent-runtime-linux-x64.tar.zst
+
+python3 -B tools/chatgpt-project-agent/prepare-project-files.py \
+  --runtime-archive /tmp/teasescript-chatgpt-project-agent-runtime-linux-x64.tar.zst \
+  --research-archive /path/to/TeaseScript-AI-Research-Archive.zip \
+  --output-directory /tmp/teasescript-chatgpt-project-files
+```
+
+The resulting folder contains at most five stable files. Uploading those files
+and copying `PROJECT-SYSTEM-PROMPT.txt` into the separate project settings field
+remain explicit manual synchronization steps recorded in issue #208.
